{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:57:11.049291+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"NONE","body":"I ran two additional controlled experiments in separate clean Python processes.\n\n### 1. Remove only the per-invocation stream creation\n\nI removed:\n\n```python\nstream = getattr(torch, DEVICE.type).Stream()\ngetattr(torch, DEVICE.type).set_stream(stream)\n```\n\nMemory accumulation became substantially slower, but the benchmark still failed at `N=10240`:\n\n```text\nN=9984 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=11730 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=9984 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=11886 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=9984 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=11886 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=10112 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=12198 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=10112 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=12356 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=10112 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=12356 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=10240 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=12672 MiB free=0 MiB\n```\n\nWithout this change, the benchmark failed much earlier, around `N=3712`. This suggests that creating a new stream for every benchmark invocation aggravates the accumulation, but is not the only cause.\n \n### 2. Remove the stream creation and clear unused cached memory between cases\n\nI then added the following at the beginning of `benchmark`, before allocating `x`:\n\n```python\ntorch.cuda.synchronize()\ntorch.cuda.empty_cache()\n```\n\nThe complete benchmark finished successfully through `N=12672`.  Memory at the beginning of every case remained stable:\n\n```text\nN=256 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\nN=256 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\nN=256 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\n...\nN=12672 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\nN=12672 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\nN=12672 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\n```\n\nMy current interpretation is that the monotonically increasing tensor shapes leave cached blocks that cannot be reused by later, larger shapes. Creating a different stream for each case makes this behavior considerably worse.\n\nSince this was reproduced on Windows/WDDM, the allocator behavior may be platform-specific. Would clearing unused cached memory between benchmark configurations, reusing one stream, or reducing the benchmark sweep be the preferred fix for this tutorial?","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:48:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661#issuecomment-5604694767","id":5604694767,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAWaHXs8AAAABThDa7w","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/5604694767/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-09-09T15:48:46Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/5604694767","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124751146?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/404-notfoundjdx","id":124751146,"login":"404-notfoundjdx","node_id":"U_kgDOB2-NKg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Describe the bug\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nRunning `python/tutorials/02-fused-softmax.py` in a clean Python process causes a CUDA out-of-memory error on a 6 GiB RTX 3060 Laptop GPU.\n\nThe largest benchmark shape (`M=4096, N=12672`) succeeds when tested alone. However, the complete shape sweep fails during the `naive_softmax` benchmark around `N=3712`.\n\nInstrumentation shows that active allocated memory remains around 16 MiB between benchmark cases, while reserved memory increases across cases:\n\n```text\nN=256 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=42 MiB free=5060 MiB\nN=256 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=318 MiB free=4772 MiB\nN=256 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=594 MiB free=4496 MiB\n...\nN=3584 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=12278 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=3712 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=12448 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=3712 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=12506 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=3712 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=12564 MiB free=0 MiB\n```\n\nThis suggests that memory is accumulating across benchmark cases rather than the largest input being too large by itself.\n\nThe fused-softmax benchmark creates and sets a new stream inside every benchmark invocation:\n\n```python\nstream = getattr(torch, DEVICE.type).Stream()\ngetattr(torch, DEVICE.type).set_stream(stream)\n```\n\nI suspect that repeatedly creating streams may prevent allocations made by `triton.testing.do_bench` from being reused across benchmark cases. I have not yet confirmed this as the root cause.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Check out Triton commit`2074a1b8a5cd283ce584f8ebca825c4f0b215fc1`.\n2. Run the tutorial in a clean Python process:\n```powershell\n$env:MPLBACKEND = \"Agg\"\npython python/tutorials/02-fused-softmax.py\n```\n3. Observe the CUDA OOM during `naive_softmax`.\nTo observe the accumulation, add this before allocating `x` inside `benchmark`:\n```python\nfree, total = torch.cuda.mem_get_info()\nprint(\n    f\"N={N} provider={provider} \"\n    f\"allocated={torch.cuda.memory_allocated() / 2**20:.0f} MiB \"\n    f\"reserved={torch.cuda.memory_reserved() / 2**20:.0f} MiB \"\n    f\"free={free / 2**20:.0f} MiB\",\n    flush=True,\n)\n```\n### Expected behavior\nThe benchmark should reuse or release temporary allocations between benchmark cases and complete when each individual input shape fits in GPU memory.\n\n### Error\n\n```text\ntorch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: out of memory\n```\n\nThe exception is reported by `di.synchronize()` inside `triton.testing.do_bench`, while benchmarking `naive_softmax`.\n\n### Environment details\n\nOS: Windows 11 10.0.26200\nPython: 3.13.15\nPyTorch: 2.11.0+cu130\nTriton: 3.6.0\nCUDA runtime: 13.0\nGPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU\nGPU memory: 6 GiB\nTutorial source commit: `2074a1b8a5cd283ce584f8ebca825c4f0b215fc1`","closed_at":"2026-09-24T20:09:34Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24322263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ThomasRaoux","id":24322263,"login":"ThomasRaoux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzIyMjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux","user_view_type":"public"},"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661/comments","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:16:16Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661/events","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661","id":5401324247,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"fc2929","default":true,"description":null,"id":125679820,"name":"bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMjU2Nzk4MjA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/labels/bug"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOAWaHXs8AAAABQfGq1w","number":11661,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton","state":"closed","state_reason":"completed","sub_issues_summary":{"completed":0,"percent_completed":0,"total":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661/timeline","title":"[BUG] Fused softmax tutorial benchmark accumulates reserved CUDA memory across benchmark cases","type":null,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T20:09:34Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124751146?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/fol