:"I ran two additional controlled experiments in separate clean Python processes.\n\n### 1. Remove only the per-invocation stream creation\n\nI removed:\n\n```python\nstream = getattr(torch, DEVICE.type).Stream()\ngetattr(torch, DEVICE.type).set_stream(stream)\n```\n\nMemory accumulation became substantially slower, but the benchmark still failed at `N=10240`:\n\n```text\nN=9984 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=11730 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=9984 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=11886 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=9984 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=11886 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=10112 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=12198 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=10112 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=12356 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=10112 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=12356 MiB free=0 MiB\nN=10240 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=12672 MiB free=0 MiB\n```\n\nWithout this change, the benchmark failed much earlier, around `N=3712`. This suggests that creating a new stream for every benchmark invocation aggravates the accumulation, but is not the only cause.\n \n### 2. Remove the stream creation and clear unused cached memory between cases\n\nI then added the following at the beginning of `benchmark`, before allocating `x`:\n\n```python\ntorch.cuda.synchronize()\ntorch.cuda.empty_cache()\n```\n\nThe complete benchmark finished successfully through `N=12672`.  Memory at the beginning of every case remained stable:\n\n```text\nN=256 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\nN=256 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\nN=256 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\n...\nN=12672 provider=triton allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\nN=12672 provider=torch allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\nN=12672 provider=naive_softmax allocated=16 MiB reserved=20 MiB free=5082 MiB\n```\n\nMy current interpretation is that the monotonically increasing tensor shapes leave cached blocks that cannot be reused by later, larger shapes. Creating a different stream for each case makes this behavior considerably worse.\n\nSince this was reproduced on Windows/WDDM, the allocator behavior may be platform-specific. Would clearing unused cached memory between benchmark configurations, reusing one stream, or reducing the benchmark sweep be the preferred fix for this tutorial?","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:48:46Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661#issuecomment-5604694767","id":5604694767,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/11661","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAWaHXs8AAAABThDa7w","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/5604694767/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-09-09T15:48:46Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/5604694767","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124751146?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/404-notfoundjdx","id":124751146,"login":"404-notfoundjdx","node_id":"U_kgDOB2-NKg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/404-notfoundjdx/subscriptions","type":"User","url